d1509d70ba098729693be3d580956d77"} {"question" "q-11717" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- For the matrix $H$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(H)=5\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 0=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(H)=0,$ we conclude that $H$ is not invertible. Since $H$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $H$ is singular.\n\n- For the matrix $J$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(J)=2\\cdot 6-3\\cdot 4=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(J)=0,$ we conclude that $J$ is not invertible. Since $J$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $J$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $K$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\nTherefore, only $H$ and $J$ is singular." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047472/state.json" "file_sha256" "60cdfec1ab8494e59e4e9a97bdc4a9d9d1509d70ba098729693be3d580956d77"} {"question" "q-11717" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047472/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ebdb28693b9dc6b25c0ef810cdaabe9a0486f1684a20e24b1ca90fc4b87cba50"} {"question" "q-11717" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047472/state.json" "file_sha256" "60cdfec1ab8494e59e4e9a97bdc4a9d9d1509d70ba098729693be3d580956d77"} {"question" "q-11717" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$H$ and $J$ only"] ["text" "$H$ and $K$ only"] ["text" "$H$ only"] ["text" "$J$ and $K$ only"] ["text" "$J$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047472/state.json" "file_sha256" "60cdfec1ab8494e59e4e9a97bdc4a9d9d1509d70ba098729693be3d580956d77"} {"question" "q-11717" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$H$ and $J$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047472/state.json" "file_sha256" "60cdfec1ab8494e59e4e9a97bdc4a9d9d1509d70ba098729693be3d580956d77"} {"question" "q-127899" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}k-1 & k-1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047472/state.json" "file_sha256" "60cdfec1ab8494e59e4e9a97bdc4a9d9d1509d70ba098729693be3d580956d77"} {"question" "q-127899" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $A$ is singular if and only if $det(A)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =(k-1)\\cdot (-1)-(k-1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-k+1-3k+3 \\\\  & =-4k+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4k+4 & =0 \\\\ k & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $k$ is $k=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047472/state.json" "file_sha256" "60cdfec1ab8494e59e4e9a97bdc4a9d9d1509d70ba098729693be3d580956d77"} {"question" "q-127899" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047472/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ebdb28693b9dc6b25c0ef810cdaabe9a0486f1684a20e24b1ca90fc4b87cba50"} {"question" "q-127899" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047472/state.json" "file_sha256" "60cdfec1ab8494e59e4e9a97bdc4a9d9d1509d70ba098729693be3d580956d77"} {"question" "q-127899" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "k=-1"] ["math" "k=-3"] ["math" "k=0"] ["math" "k=1"] ["math" "k=3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047472/state.json" "file_sha256" "60cdfec1ab8494e59e4e9a97bdc4a9d9d1509d70ba098729693be3d580956d77"} {"question" "q-127899" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "k=1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047472/state.json" "file_sha256" "60cdfec1ab8494e59e4e9a97bdc4a9d9d1509d70ba098729693be3d580956d77"} {"question" "q-127906" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $M=[\\begin{aligned}t & 2 \\\\ t & -8\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047472/state.json" "file_sha256" "60cdfec1ab8494e59e4e9a97bdc4a9d9d1509d70ba098729693be3d580956d77"} {"question" "q-127906" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $M$ is singular if and only if $det(M)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =t\\cdot (-8)-t\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-8t-2t \\\\  & =-10t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10t & =0 \\\\ t & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $t$ is $t=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047472/state.json" "file_sha256" "60cdfec1ab8494e59e4e9a97bdc4a9d9d1509d70ba098729693be3d580956d77"} {"question" "q-127906" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047472/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ebdb28693b9dc6b25c0ef810cdaabe9a0486f1684a20e24b1ca90fc4b87cba50"} {"question" "q-127906" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047472/state.json" "file_sha256" "60cdfec1ab8494e59e4e9a97bdc4a9d9d1509d70ba098729693be3d580956d77"} {"question" "q-127906" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "t=0"] ["math" "t=4"] ["math" "t=5"] ["math" "t=\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "t=\\frac{1}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047472/state.json" "file_sha256" "60cdfec1ab8494e59e4e9a97bdc4a9d9d1509d70ba098729693be3d580956d77"} {"question" "q-127906" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "t=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047472/state.json" "file_sha256" "60cdfec1ab8494e59e4e9a97bdc4a9d9d1509d70ba098729693be3d580956d77"} {"question" "q-313957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $B=[\\begin{aligned}x-4 & 1 \\\\ 7 & x+2\\end{aligned}]$\nbe a singular matrix. **In ascending order**, the values of $x$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047472/state.json" "file_sha256" "60cdfec1ab8494e59e4e9a97bdc4a9d9d1509d70ba098729693be3d580956d77"} {"question" "q-313957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(x-4)\\cdot (x+2)-7\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-2x-8-7 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-2x-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x-15 & =0 \\\\ (x+3)(x-5) & =0 \\\\ x & =-3,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the values of $x$ are\n\n$$\nx=-3\\,\\text{and}\\,x=5.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047472/state.json" "file_sha256" "60cdfec1ab8494e59e4e9a97bdc4a9d9d1509d70ba098729693be3d580956d77"} {"question" "q-313957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047472/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ebdb28693b9dc6b25c0ef810cdaabe9a0486f1684a20e24b1ca90fc4b87cba50"} {"question" "q-313957" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047472/state.json" "file_sha256" "60cdfec1ab8494e59e4e9a97bdc4a9d9d1509d70ba098729693be3d580956d77"} {"question" "q-313957" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047472/state.json" "file_sha256" "60cdfec1ab8494e59e4e9a97bdc4a9d9d1509d70ba098729693be3d580956d77"} {"question" "q-313957" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047472/state.json" "fil